.TH DANBY-FISHINGONE 1
.SH NAME
danby-fishingone \- bioeconomics of a single fish stock
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/fishingone
.SH MODEL
X'=rX(1-X/K)-qEX;
E'=sE(pqX-c).
.PP
X is fish biomass and E fishing effort.  Harvest is qEX.  Effort expands when
revenue per effort pqX exceeds cost c and contracts when fishing is unprofitable.
The open-access equilibrium has X*=c/(pq) and
E*=r(1-X*/K)/q when X* lies below carrying capacity.
.SH DISPLAY
Stock and effort histories show the ecological-economic feedback: depletion
reduces profit, falling effort permits recovery, and delayed response can
produce cycles.  This replaces the constant-take harvest demonstration for
the economics section.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag either state bar.  Tracks set growth, carrying capacity, catchability,
price, cost, and effort response.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and
q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The analytic open-access equilibrium is checked by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/fishingone.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/fishingone.b
